  "notes": "Block-13 cause code A governs category (Personnel Error) despite the hardware degradation narrative; theme captures both PM-program and human-performance/communication angles. SGT is modeled as a backup because the narrative states it 'would have automatically started and would have been able to maintain vacuum' during the postulated accident scenario used in the engineering review, treated here as an operable safety-function backstop supporting the no-loss-of-safety-function conclusion. Primary Containment (NH) and penetration (PEN) are mentioned only as background/design context describing Secondary Containment's structure, not as participants in the failure chain; PEN component node retained per EIIS mention but not linked into chain since it plays no explicit failure role. Three previous similar occurrences captured as stub LERs with keys exactly as stated in narrative (no unit digit prefix given in text)."
